@startuml
title CycleFar — Manual Intervals.icu reconciliation

autonumber
hide footbox

actor Rider
boundary "IntervalsIcuSyncsController" as Controller
control "SyncNextTwo" as Sync
control "WorkoutSerializer" as Serializer
control "IntervalsIcu::Client" as Client
database "PostgreSQL" as Database
participant "Intervals.icu" as Remote

Rider -> Controller: POST manual sync
Controller -> Database: resolve signed-in rider's active plan
Controller -> Sync: SyncNextTwo.new(plan: owned active plan).call
Sync -> Database: resolve plan owner's profile (default initializer input)
group owner session advisory lock (Synchronization; released in ensure)
Sync -> Database: acquire owner advisory lock; reload plan\nreject unless still active
Sync -> Sync: validate profile owner and API key
Sync -> Database: select next two planned structured workouts/openers\nfrom today; exclude time off
Database --> Sync: eligible set (zero, one or two workouts)
loop each selected workout
  Sync -> Serializer: payload(canonical steps, current FTP, stable external ID)
  Serializer --> Sync: event payload
end
group local transaction before HTTP
  Sync -> Database: retain owned identities for selected workouts\nnew identities have no confirmed event ID/digest/timestamp
end

alt eligible set is not empty
  Sync -> Client: upsert_events(payloads)
  Client -> Remote: POST athlete/0/events/bulk?upsert=true
  alt upload fails or outcome is uncertain
    Remote --> Client: error or timeout
    Client --> Sync: mapped error after transient retry where applicable
    break stop before cleanup
      Sync -> Database: release owner advisory lock in ensure
      Sync --> Controller: error; retain identities and prior confirmed metadata
    end
  else upload confirmed
    Remote --> Client: returned events with external IDs and event IDs
    Client --> Sync: events
  end
else eligible set is empty
  Sync -> Sync: skip upload; continue stale cleanup
end

group following successful upload or empty-set selection
  group local transaction
    Sync -> Database: save confirmed selected event IDs, digests and timestamps
  end
  Sync -> Database: load all this rider's sync records outside selected set\nincluding missed/completed, past-moved, deleted and previous-plan
  Database --> Sync: stale owned external IDs
  opt stale set is not empty
    Sync -> Client: delete_events(stale external IDs)
    Client -> Remote: PUT athlete/0/events/bulk-delete
    alt cleanup fails
      Remote --> Client: error or timeout
      Client --> Sync: mapped error after transient retry where applicable
      Sync -> Database: release owner advisory lock in ensure
      Sync --> Controller: PartialSyncError; keep confirmed uploads and stale identities
    else cleanup confirmed (missing events ignored upstream)
      Remote --> Client: delete response
      Client --> Sync: deletion confirmed
      group local transaction
        Sync -> Database: destroy stale sync records
      end
      Sync -> Database: release owner advisory lock in ensure
      Sync --> Controller: synced and removed counts
    end
  end
  opt no stale records
    Sync -> Database: release owner advisory lock in ensure
    Sync --> Controller: synced count; zero removed
  end
end
end
Controller --> Rider: redirect to calendar with result or retry/error guidance

note over Sync, Remote
  Remote requests and local transactions are separate.
  Stable cyclefar-workout-<id> IDs make retries idempotent.
  Selected moved workouts are upserted with their original identity.
  Only this rider's tracked calendar events are reconciled.
  Sync rechecks active status under the owner lock shared with PlanRemover.
  Removal cannot interleave cleanup with an in-flight sync.
  Sync uses existing structured detail without materialising outlines.
  No remote listing, unrelated-event edits or activity/history API calls.
  Local completed workouts, steps, snapshots and feedback remain immutable.
end note
@enduml
